Click + Add MQTT device
It'll ask for a device name first (e.g. "Audio BPM") — this is just a container/grouping, not an entity itself
After creating the device, you'll get an option to add an entity to it — choose Sensor
Fill in the entity form:
Name: BPM Debounced
State topic: bifrost/audio/bpm
Unit of measurement: bpm
Device class: None
Expand Advanced settings (or it may just show more fields below without a separate expander in this version) → Value template field → paste:

     {% set new_bpm = value | float(0) %}
     {% set old_bpm = this.state | float(0) if this.state not in ['unknown','unavailable',none] else 0 %}
     {% if old_bpm == 0 or (new_bpm - old_bpm) | abs >= 4 %}
       {{ new_bpm }}
     {% else %}
       {{ old_bpm }}
     {% endif %}

